"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"The PR says to \"Bind visibleRowsHeight only to layoutSerial\" and reports \"walked_once 231\". In QML a binding depends on every property it reads while evaluating, including reads inside the JS functions it calls. rowListHeight (Menu.qml:206) and dmenuRowListHeight (:228) still loop on `i < displayModel.count`, so count remains a dependency and each per-row append (:628, :734) re-runs the walk. The PR body itself says reads inside the walk \"remain binding dependencies\". In this run report-reproducers.test.mjs passed while expecting the real-engine KI reproducer to exit 1 with 'DEFECT: 231-row menu open'. The KI evidence (known_issue_reproduced) was refreshed by the mirror. Our manual qml6 differential, outside the package, measured 232 passes / 27,027 visits at base and at head. No typed test outcome exists for the PR's purpose.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":120},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":228},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":734},{"id":"test/node/report-reproducers.test.mjs","kind":"test"},{"id":"test/reports/report-cmulr8ysi0jwr1gw4fjmt9khq.sh","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"proof/known-issues/KI-MENU-OPEN-QUADRATIC.yaml","kind":"file","line":25}],"severity":"high","title":"Question: does the PR remove the quadratic walk at all? The evidence says it does not","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Real-engine cost witness for menu open\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"detail":"menu-shell runs every extra test/shell.d/menu-*-test.sh (proof.yaml), so the PR's test is now its own JUnit testcase in this run. testResults reports 56/56 passed, and the test carries no requirement tag. The test regex-checks the Menu.qml binding and signatures. It then asserts simulate(231,false).walked == 231 against a JS function it defines itself, and never evaluates the QML binding. So it passes while the real engine still walks 27,027 rows. I re-ran it at the evaluated commit: 13 ok lines, exit 0. Opinion: its final assertion name 'menu height no longer scales with the square of row count' overstates what it checks.","refs":[{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-height-quadratic-test.sh","kind":"file","line":80},{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-height-quadratic-test.sh","kind":"file","line":89},{"id":"proof.yaml","kind":"file","line":173}],"severity":"medium","title":"The PR's own test now runs in the audit and passes, but pins only source text and a JS simulation","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"claim":{"params":{"candidate":"unmapped_code|test/shell.d/menu-height-quadratic-test.sh","path":"test/shell.d/menu-height-quadratic-test.sh","position":"spec_gap"},"type":"unmapped_code"},"detail":"This is our audit position, not an oversight. The test asserts source text and a JS simulation, not a requirement's behaviour. The behaviour it targets is intended: #10601 reports its absence, and KI-MENU-OPEN-QUADRATIC's remediation says \"Also add a requirement that bounds the menu-open cost; none exists today\". B757 states only the fold geometry, not how often it is computed. Position spec_gap: add a requirement that bounds height passes per rebuild (for example, at most 2 walks per row). Witness it with a real-engine counter, such as the KI reproducer, not this test. That requirement would be violated at this head, because the PR leaves the 232 passes / 27,027 visits unchanged. Tracing this test to it as-is would record a check that cannot fail on the defect.","refs":[{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-height-quadratic-test.sh","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-B757","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"proof/known-issues/KI-MENU-OPEN-QUADR