-260929-B8N9","kind":"requirement"}],"method":"review.changes (spec, code-trace, function and call-level requirement impact)","note":"SW-REQ-260929-B8N9 is in review.changes (code_changed, matchLevel file).","status":"confirmed"}},{"detail":"The unobserved 'test' is test:shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:237:item, the product function item(). No runner will ever produce a JUnit outcome for it. B8N9's other 2 verifying tests passed, including menu-pointer-lifecycle-test.sh. Its boundary, error_handling and malformed_input cells are observed_pass. The fix belongs to the engine's scanner, not to this PR. The disclosure still prevents readiness.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":237},{"id":"SW-REQ-260929-B8N9","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-pointer-lifecycle-test.sh","kind":"test"}],"severity":"info","title":"test_outcome_unobserved:SW-REQ-260929-B8N9 is the same item() artefact; the real witness passed","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"review.behaviorDiff ran 213 inputs over the corpus, data, lifecycle, scale and timing partitions and found 0 differences. Its harness (test/bdiff/harness.mjs) drives MenuModel.js JSONC parsing and the request lifecycle, never the visibleRowsHeight binding. The PR's stated goal is performance, so a missing COST partition matters. Our manual qml6 differential (outside the package) found 0 height differences and identical pass/visit counts on the headline input. These results cannot be typed as behavior_changed claims.","refs":[{"id":"test/bdiff/harness.mjs","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":120}],"severity":"medium","title":"The configured differential has no height or cost partition, so 0 differences is no evidence for this change","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:rowListHeight","shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:rebuildDisplay"],"scenario":"open a 20-row search with the divider shown, then cancel() and toggle searchDivider without a rebuild; compare visibleRowsHeight to a fresh rebuild"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"The explicit args used to carry dependencies. Invalidation now relies on reads inside the bodies: displayModel.count/get(i), root.filterText via rowHeightForDetail (only when count>0), root.mode, dmenuMaxHeight, and panel geometry. searchDivider is truly dropped. Today it is written only on rebuild paths (Menu.qml:609, :679, :704), which then bump layoutSerial (:735). cancel() clears filterText without a rebuild (:906). Our manual run found no stale height. A future writer that toggles the divider without a rebuild would leave the height stale.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":120},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":735},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":906},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-TKDP","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"low","title":"Question: with searchDivider no longer a dependency, can any state change leave a stale height?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Stale-height probe for state changes without a rebuild\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"detail":"Menu.qml:668-673. The PR says: \"When rebuildDisplay returns early because rows are not loaded, bump layoutSerial so the card collapses without relying on a count binding.\" It adds one binding evaluation. Before, the base invalidated through count. The bump is harmless, but correctness does not need it while the bodies still read count.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":671},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-TKDP","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"low","title":"The new rowsLoaded=false serial bump is intended, and the PR states it","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"Menu.qml:117-119 (\"Height must not bind to displayModel.count ... one pass is enough\") and :197 tell maintainers that the binding depends on layoutSerial alone. Reads inside the called functions are tracked too, so the comments are inaccurate and suggest the quadratic walk is fixed when it is not.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":117},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":197}],"severity":"low","title":"Opinion: the new code comments describe a QML dependency model that does not hold","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"review.effects is absent for this QML change. No new_call_path or reachable_from claim can be checked, and uncodified connections cannot be detected. From reading the code: visibleRowsHeight feeds only cardHeight, and the height functions are called only from that binding. The engine has not verified this.","refs":[{"id":"review.effects.approximations","kind":"check"},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":120}],"severity":"info","title":"Change effects were not analyzed (effects_unavailable): the package has no QML effect or caller facts","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}}],"packageDigest":"sha256:2c95bf6fcc9ccb823cbf64daeee0165ef2574b5e9cfdfac0b415e3ec0cc9c54b","packageIdentity":"epkg-f4bb61cd145f99129d783ed768c40c3d1d5cab1e5ed85fd33df016de27461e23","riskAssessment":{"level":"medium","rationale":"Height values look unchanged: our manual qml6 differential found no differences, but the package's own differential does not cover heights. The PR does not meet its stated purpose: the quadratic open cost remains, and the KI reproducer still reports it. The PR's new test cannot detect that, and the new comments could hide it. One compatibility finding is open and unapproved (an engine witness artefact in my reading). This review is advisory only."},"schemaVersion":"reqproof.review-annotation.v1","suggestedTests":[{"forClaim":2,"rationale":"In qml6 offscreen, run the visibleRowsHeight binding with rebuildDmenuDisplay/rebuildDisplay for 231 rows. Assert at most 2 height passes and at most 2n row visits, and trace the test to a new cost requirement. The KI reproducer's counter does this already, and it fails at the head as it does at the base.","refs":[{"id":"test/reports/report-cmulr8ysi0jwr1gw4fjmt9khq.sh","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":120}],"title":"Real-engine cost witness for menu open"},{"forClaim":8,"rationale":"Change state without a rebuild: toggle searchDivider, clear the filter with cancel(), and change dmenuMaxHeight and panel geometry. After each change, assert visibleRowsHeight equals its value after a fresh rebuild.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":120}],"title":"Stale-height probe for state changes without a rebuild"}],"summary":"**What the PR does.** Upstream #10631 (fresh3nough, fixes #10601) binds `visibleRowsHeight` to `rowListHeight(layoutSerial)` / `dmenuRowListHeight(layoutSerial)` and drops the count/filter/divider args (Menu.qml:120). It bumps `layoutSerial` on the `!rowsLoaded` early return (:671) and adds test/shell.d/menu-height-quadratic-test.sh. The later mirror commits are our proof work, not upstream's: a KI-MENU-OPEN-QUADRATIC note, a trace re-review of the Menu.qml-linked requirements, and an evidence refresh.\n\n**Is the fix verified?** No, and the purpose is not achieved. QML tracks every property read while a binding evaluates, including reads inside the functions it calls. Both height functions still loop on `displayModel.count` (:206, :228), so each append still re-runs the walk. In this run report-reproducers.test.mjs passed while still expecting the KI reproducer to exit 1 ('DEFECT: 231-row menu open'). Our manual qml6 differential (outside the package) found 232 passes / 27,027 visits at both base and head, with identical heights. The PR's test now runs in menu-shell (56/56 JUnit passed) but checks only source text and a JS simulation. Diff coverage: no changed decision lines.\n\n**Compatibility.** cf-c8dd4255b9f5771b (mcdc_diff, unapproved, prevents ready): the base B8N9 'witness' Menu.qml:233:item is gone at the head. That witness is the product function item(): engine 650534c2 counts any name starting with 'it' as a test. item() is byte-identical and moved to :237 under 4 added lines. I read this as an id artefact, not a behaviour change. Only a human reviewer can approve it. The auditor's accept note is not an approval. The configured differential (213 inputs, 0 differences) has no height or cost partition.\n\n**Questions for a human.** Should this merge as the fix for #10601 when the quadratic walk remains? Is implicit read tracking acceptable now that searchDivider is no longer a dependency?\n\n**Traceability.** rowListHeight / dmenuRowListHeight trace to SW-REQ-260922-B757 (function level). 27 more requirements are code_changed through file-level traces. The PR test is unmapped on purpose: no requirement bounds menu-open cost, and this head does not meet such a bound (spec_gap). effects_unavailable.\n\n**Not caused by this PR.** test_outcome_unobserved:SW-REQ-260929-B8N9 comes from the same item() artefact; the real witness menu-pointer-lifecycle-test.sh passed. Readiness: not_assessed. Next decision: human_judgement (compat_changes_unapproved)."}
